examples.solution_text:
The denominator is zero at $x=-2$, so this input is excluded.
For $x>-2$, $|x+2|=x+2$:
$\begin{aligned}f(x)&=\frac{x+2}{x+2}\\&=1\end{aligned}$
For $x<-2$, $|x+2|=-(x+2)$:
$\begin{aligned}f(x)&=\frac{-(x+2)}{x+2}\\&=-1\end{aligned}$
Therefore $f(x)=\begin{cases}-1,&x<-2\\1,&x>-2\end{cases}$.
Domain: $(-\infty,-2)\cup(-2,\infty)$. Range: $\{-1,1\}$.
Draw horizontal rays with open endpoints because $f(-2)$ is undefined.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=12mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-1.8)--(0,1.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[mathblue,thick,<-] (-4.7,-1)--(-2,-1);
\draw[mathblue,thick,->] (-2,1)--(1.7,1);
\draw[mathblue,fill=white] (-2,-1) circle (2pt);
\draw[mathblue,fill=white] (-2,1) circle (2pt);
\path (-2,-1) node[below] {$(-2,-1)$} (-2,1) node[above] {$(-2,1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For $x\ge0$, $|x|=x$:
$\begin{aligned}f(x)&=2x+2x\\&=4x\end{aligned}$
For $x<0$, $|x|=-x$:
$\begin{aligned}f(x)&=2x+2(-x)\\&=0\end{aligned}$
Therefore $f(x)=\begin{cases}0,&x<0\\4x,&x\ge0\end{cases}$.
The branches meet at $(0,0)$. Draw a horizontal ray to the left and a ray of gradient $4$ to the right.
Domain: $(-\infty,\infty)$. Range: $[0,\infty)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (-3,0)--(2.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.8)--(0,6.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[mathblue,thick,<-] (-2.8,0)--(0,0);
\draw[mathblue,thick,->] (0,0)--(1.5,6);
\fill[mathblue] (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[mathblue] (1,4) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[below right] {$(0,0)$} (1,4) node[right] {$(1,4)$} (-1.5,0) node[above] {$y=0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
